# Build output. Anchored with a leading slash: a bare "mrw" would match any
# path component of that name and silently exclude cmd/mrw/ — it did, for two
# commits.
/bin/
/mrw

# The working set is per-developer state, not project config.
/.mrw/

# Two artifacts were committed under `git add -A` before ADR-004 landed, and
# neither was noticed because nothing here excluded them:
#   internal/state/relative/...  a state directory a pre-guard mrw resolved
#                               from a RELATIVE XDG_STATE_HOME, against the
#                               package's own working directory
#   tmp/claude-501/.../mrw-mutant  a Mach-O binary from another machine's
#                               scratchpad
# The first is impossible now (state.stateHome refuses a relative value and
# TestRelativeXDGStateHomeLeavesNothingBehind holds it); the second was never
# possible to prevent in code. Both paths are excluded so a stray copy cannot
# come back the same way.
/tmp/
/internal/state/relative/

# Compiled Python from .claude/hooks/rules-on-read.py. A `py_compile` check
# during ADR-022 left rules-on-read.cpython-314.pyc beside the hook and
# `git add -A .claude` swept it into a commit (review of #88): a build
# artefact tied to one interpreter version, and the class of file ADR-004
# exists to keep out of the tree.
__pycache__/
